	<div class="content">
		<h2>Introduction:</h2>
		<p class="intro">Drexel's meal plans provide a flexible and convenient way to manage student meals. But the more option student have, the more questions students may have regarding which meal plan to choose. To help students make a wise decision, here are all the meal plan options Drexel provides to freshmen and upperclassman and graduate students. Drexel freshmen have 3 options. Drexel upperclassmen and graduate students have 7 more options other than the 3 options they can choose.</p>

                <!--dining halls--!>
                <!--dining halls--!>
		<iframe src = "https://images.elevate-dxp.com/adobe/assets/urn:aaid:aem:53b09e92-4a99-4573-9d5e-fc9971d6c6aa/as/_0180618_230727.webp?width=600&crop=0p,0.19p,100p,99.62p" title = "urban eatery" style="height: 300px; width: 600px"></iframe>

		<h2>First Year Plans:</h2>
		<div class = "itemBar">
			<div class = "item options">
				<h2>Weekly 14 + 250 Dining</h2>
				<ul>
					<li>$2,210</li>
					<li>Meal Swipes: 14 meals each week</li>
					<li>Dining Dollars: $250 per term</li>
					<li>Guest meal: 2</li>
				</ul>
			</div>

			<div class = "item options">
				<h2>All Access + 225 Dining Dollars</h2>
				<ul>
					<li>$2,380</li>
					<li>Meal Swipes: Unlimited</li>
					<li>Dining Dollars: $225 per term</li>
					<li>Guest meal: 2</li>
				</ul>
			</div>

			<div class = "item options">
				<h2>All Access + 200 Dining Dollars</h2>
				<ul>
					<li>$2,565</li>
					<li>Meal Swipes: Unlimited</li>
					<li>Dining Dollars: $400 per term</li>
					<li>Guest meal: 2</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</div>

			<h2>Important Information:</h2>

			<div class = "intro">
				<ul>
					<li>Unused Dining dollars will transfer to the next term if students have purchased the next term dining plan before the deadline. </li>
					<li>Unused meal swipes will not transfer to the next term, so be cautious of unused meal swipes.</li>
					<li>Meal exchange: You can use 1 meal per meal period to exchange meals at the Perelman Center for Jewish Life Cafe.</li>
					<li>All plans above allow meal exchange at The Perelman Center for Jewish Life.</li>
					<li>All plans above have 2 meals for guests each term. Students can invite their friends or family outside or inside the school to enjoy the meal with them. </li>
				</ul>

			<h3>Which to choose?</h3>
			<div class = "intro">
				<ul>
					<li>Not a breakfast person? Choose Weekly 14! You can have dinner and lunch every day.</li>
					<li>Breakfast person? Choose All Access, and you can access as many meals as you like.</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</div>
		<h1>Upperclassman and Graduate Students:</h1>
		<p class="intro">Upperclassman and Graduate Students can choose any of the freshman meal plan options, and also:</p>
		<div class = "dining_option">
			<div class = "item options">
				<h2>150 Dining Dollars</h2>
				<p>Price: $150 per term</p>
				<p>Dining Dollars: $150 per term</p>
			</div>
                        <div class = "item options">
                                <h2>250 Dining Dollars</h2>
                                <p>Price: $250 per term</p>
                                <p>Dining Dollars: $250 per term</p>
                        </div>
                        <div class = "item options">
                                <h2>500 Dining Dollars</h2>
                                <p>Price: $500 per term</p>
                                <p>Dining Dollars: $500 per term</p>
                        </div>
                        <div class = "item options">
                                <h2>800 Dining Dollars</h2>
                                <p>Price: $800 per term</p>
                                <p>Dining Dollars: $800 per term</p>
                        </div>
		</div>

		<div class = "intro">
			<ul>
				<li>If you can’t finish your dining dollars by the end of each term, the unused dollars will roll over to the next term only if you purchase the next term's dining plan.</li>
				<li>If you don’t plan to purchase a dining plan for next term, make sure to finish all your unused dining dollars!</li>
			</ul>
		</div>
		
		</br>
                <div class = "dining_option">
                        <div class = "item options">
                                <h2>Block 25 + 200 Dining Dollars</h2>
                                <p>Price: $570 per term</p>
                                <p>Dining Dollars: $200 per term</p>
				<p>Meal Swipes: 25 per term</p>
				<p>Cost per meal swipes(exclude dining dollars: $14.80</p>
                        </div>
                        <div class = "item options">
                                <h2>Block 25 + 200 Dining Dollars</h2>
                                <p>Price: $1,020 per term</p>
                                <p>Dining Dollars: $350 per term</p>
				<p>Meal Swipes: 50 per term</p>
                                <p>Cost per meal swipes(exclude dining dollars: $13.40</p>

                        </div>
                        <div class = "item options">
                                <h2>Block 25 + 500 Dining Dollars</h2>
                                <p>Price: $1,470 per term</p>
                                <p>Dining Dollars: $500 per term</p>
                                <p>Meal Swipes: 80 per term</p>
                                <p>Cost per meal swipes(exclude dining dollars: $12.13</p>
                        </div>
                </div>
	
		<div class = "intro"> 
			<ul>
				<li>All can exchange meals at the Perelman Center for Jewish Life using meal swipes (One meal swipe per exchange).</li>
				<li>Choose any of these if you want to have food in the dining hall occasionally.</li>

			</ul>
		</div>

	</div>
